{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787966253544189587,"compiled_state":{"alias":"gangrene-dissected-nymph","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"550d40a24dc1a772d74fd3ce0c83e7bca1b3af9d6e5b4fc20976cde4bdbb7010","event_uuid":"7dc0c38d-3b5e-4bdc-9fae-6ab89af6fb07","position":{"commit_sha":"78f6971e2d7b915b031f2403fac5bbb310da3746","position":"1787961770470070471-7dc0c38d-3b5e-4bdc-9fae-6ab89af6fb07"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a2491a7a522bcd288e7cbee6bfd5adcd6a8e511efa54b9d31b2cac315139db4d","event_uuid":"ddb0df98-343a-4be4-8872-346daed5f1e2","position":{"commit_sha":"445f5b57e6bb0903d3a685ffc0277174889f6a12","position":"1787961779590375306-ddb0df98-343a-4be4-8872-346daed5f1e2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787961770470070471,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ddb0df98-343a-4be4-8872-346daed5f1e2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"aefe-614a-2631-4117"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`rapt-dreadable-dromedary` (`aefe-614a-2631-4117`) put\n`rebar._store.store_usability.store_is_usable` on the library/MCP read chokepoint\n(`_reads._tracker`). The predicate spawns `git -C <tracker> rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` on\nEVERY read.\n\nThe approved plan reasoned this was negligible because \"the read path ALREADY spawns git\n(throttled `git fetch`/reconverge via `_fresh`)\". That reasoning is not quite right: `_fresh`\nis throttled to at most once per minute, so on the great majority of reads there is NO git\nspawn today. The predicate adds an UNTHROTTLED one.\n\n## Measurement (this worktree, off `origin/main` 565e1856)\n\nA 25-ticket store, `REBAR_NO_SYNC=1`, 40 iterations, predicate neutralized by monkeypatching\n`store_usability.store_is_usable` to a constant (so only the probe is removed, not the guard):\n\n```\nlist_tickets WITH predicate:    22.7 ms\nlist_tickets WITHOUT predicate:  5.6 ms\npredicate overhead:             17.1 ms  (305%)\n```\n\nSo on a small store the probe costs roughly 4x the read itself. In absolute terms it is one\ngit process startup (~17ms on this host). On the production tracker, log reduction dominates\nand the relative cost is small; the 4x is a relative figure on an already-fast operation.\n\n## Why it was not addressed in the parent change\n\nThe parent change shipped the operator-approved, plan-review-certified design unchanged. The\ntwo obvious optimizations both have real downsides that need a deliberate decision rather than\nan in-flight one:\n\n- **Caching the verdict.** A cached \"usable\" answer is precisely the staleness hazard the\n  parent bug is about: a store that becomes unusable mid-session would keep reading as usable.\n  Any cache needs an explicit invalidation story.\n- **Resolving HEAD in-process.** Reading `.git/HEAD` and following the ref by hand\n  reimplements git ref resolution (packed-refs, `.git`-as-a-file for worktrees/submodules,\n  detached HEAD), which is fragile — and the parent change deliberately chose the\n  `footprint._git` prior-art pattern over that.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A decision is recorded (in this ticket) on whether the ~17ms per-read probe is accepted\n      as-is, or is to be reduced, and by which mechanism.\n- [ ] If reduced: the same measurement harness shows the overhead drop, AND the regression\n      tests in `tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py` still pass unchanged — the\n      broken/no-`.git`/mid-clone cases must still raise `store_uninitialized`.\n- [ ] If reduced by caching: a test proves a store that becomes unusable DURING a session is\n      detected, not served from a stale \"usable\" verdict.\n- [ ] If accepted as-is: the reasoning is recorded on `store_usability.py` so the next reader\n      does not re-litigate it.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d582-e941-96b6-41a8","ticket_type":"task","title":"store_is_usable adds an unthrottled git spawn to every read (~17ms, 4x on a small store)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7dc0c38d-3b5e-4bdc-9fae-6ab89af6fb07","ddb0df98-343a-4be4-8872-346daed5f1e2"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787966253544189587,"uuid":"f2f67f73-12dd-4d54-907f-be413a329752"}